# Changelog
## [0.4.1] — 2026-11-21
### Fixes
 - FEC limits now match the kernel data path: `FecMode`/`fec_pack` accept only
   `1 <= K <= 8` and `1 <= M <= 2`, so `K + M <= 255` is no longer the
   contract. `FEC_MAX_SHARDS` is `10`; larger fixed profiles are rejected
   instead of being emitted and refused by the kernel.
 - `ExtraPorts` documentation now states the actual default `0`, not `4`.

### Added
 - `UnderlayMtu` (40), `FecStats` (38) and `BbrStats` (39) are covered by the
   attribute table and UAPI-parity check; `FecStats`/`BbrStats` are emitted
   only in `GET_DEVICE` replies.

## [0.4.0] — 2026-11-20
### Added
 - `UWGDEVICE_A_UNDERLAY_MTU` (40) device attribute.
 - `UWGDEVICE_A_FEC_STATS` (38) and `UWGDEVICE_A_BBR_STATS` (39) nested
   attributes with `FecStats`/`BbrStats` types.

### Fixes
 - Fuzzing (`cargo-fuzz` 0.13, 10 minutes per target) found a panic in
   `UmbrawgAllowedIpAttr::parse`: an empty `UWGALLOWEDIP_A_CIDR_MASK` payload
   indexed out of bounds. It now returns `DecodeError`.
 - Magic header parsing keeps the wire representation instead of normalizing
   it to a string: 8-byte payloads become `H1Range`..`H4Range`, 4-byte payloads
   become `H1Legacy`..`H4Legacy`, so a parsed message re-emits byte for byte.
   Inverted `u64` ranges are rejected with `DecodeError`.
 - `fuzz/Cargo.toml` carries the `cargo-fuzz` metadata, so the declared targets
   build and run with `cargo fuzz`.

### New features
 - Full rustdoc coverage: every public type, variant, field and constant is
   documented, examples cover device, peer, allowed IP and range helpers;
   the crate denies missing documentation.
 - `UmbrawgDeviceConfig`: a validated builder for `UWG_CMD_SET_DEVICE`
   messages. It accepts the private key, listen port, fwmark, `Jc/Jmin/Jmax`,
   `S1`..`S4`, `H1`..`H4` as `u32` ranges, `I1`..`I5`, the header protection
   key, the `u16` tuning ranges and the UmbraWG 3.1 switches, and rejects
   invalid interface selectors, key lengths, inverted ranges, overlapping
   magic headers and unsupported flags.
 - `UmbrawgPeerConfig`: a validated builder for peer entries, covering the
   public and preshared keys, IPv4/IPv6 endpoints, persistent keepalive in
   both wire formats, allowed IPs including `UWGALLOWEDIP_F_REMOVE_ME`, peer
   flags and advanced security.
 - `UmbrawgConfigError`: typed, non-panicking errors for the builders, with
   `Display` and `std::error::Error` implementations.
 - `UmbrawgAllowedIp::new/remove/from_spec` and read accessors
   (`ip_addr`, `cidr`, `family`, `is_remove`); `FromStr` parses
   `"addr/prefix"` specs.
 - `range::u16_range_pack/unpack/to_string/from_string` for the packed
   `u16`-range wire format of the UmbraWG 3.x tuning knobs.
 - Conversions from messages and peers back into configurations:
   `UmbrawgDeviceConfig::from_message`, `UmbrawgPeerConfig::from_peer` and
   the corresponding `TryFrom` implementations.
 - 42 builder tests covering happy paths, range boundaries, invalid
   key lengths, empty lists, IPv4/IPv6 and wire round trips.

### Other
 - Constants in `constants.rs` are documented with their attribute kinds and
   wire types.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-11-16
### New features
 - Full numeric parity with the UmbraWG 3.1 UAPI (`uapi/umbrawg.h`):
   - `UmbrawgPeerAttribute::AdvancedSecurity` for
     `UWGPEER_A_ADVANCED_SECURITY` (kind 11, `NLA_FLAG`, empty payload).
   - `UmbrawgAllowedIpAttr::Flags` for `UWGALLOWEDIP_A_FLAGS` (kind 4,
     `u32`).
   - `UmbrawgCmd::UnknownPeer` for `UWG_CMD_UNKNOWN_PEER` (command 2),
     including messages that carry `UWGDEVICE_A_PEER`.
   - `constants::UWGPEER_F_HAS_ADVANCED_SECURITY`,
     `constants::UWGALLOWEDIP_F_REMOVE_ME`, `constants::UWG_CMD_*` and
     `constants::UWG_KEY_LEN`.
 - `scripts/check-uapi-parity.sh` compares `src/constants.rs` with the
   kernel header and fails on any mismatch.
 - Round-trip, wire-format and property tests for the new attributes,
   flags and command.

### Bug fixes
 - `UmbrawgAttribute::Peer` no longer emits an extra nesting level. The
   peer attributes of `UWGDEVICE_A_PEER` (`UWG_CMD_UNKNOWN_PEER`
   notifications) are nested directly, the way the kernel writes them.

### Other
 - The crate is formatted with nightly `rustfmt` and its `.rustfmt.toml`.

### CI
 - Run property tests as a separate job.
 - Build both `cargo fuzz` targets on nightly.
 - Add a preflight probe for the UmbraWG kernel family; integration tests are
   skipped as a job (with an explicit warning) when the module is unavailable.
 - Use nightly for rustfmt and clippy so unstable `.rustfmt.toml` options are
   applied consistently.

## [0.2.1] - 2026-08-25
### New features
 - Added UmbraWG 3.1 device attributes: `RandomTrailers` and
   `DisableCookies` (`u8` flags, attribute kinds 33 and 34). Only the
   UmbraWG 3.1+ kernel module accepts them; the genl family version is
   still 3.

## [0.1.2] - 2026-06-06
### Breaking changes
 - Changed `H1`..`H4` and `I1`..`I5` attribute types from `u16` to `String`
   to match the UmbraWG kernel module (`NLA_NUL_STRING`).
 - Removed unsupported `DataInit`, `DataResponse`, `DataConfirm`, and
   `DataTransport` attributes (they are not present in the kernel module).

### Bug fixes
 - `SetDevice` with magic header specs no longer returns `EINVAL`.

## [0.1.1] - 2026-06-06
### Breaking changes
 - Dropped generic `WgFamily` trait; the crate is now UmbraWG-only.
 - Renamed all public types from `Wireguard*` to `Umbrawg*` to avoid
   name collisions with the plain WireGuard crate.
 - Merged `UmbraWgAttribute` into `WireguardAttribute` (now the single
   attribute enum containing both base and Umbra-specific fields).
 - Family name hard-coded to `"umbrawg"` and version to `2`.

### New features
 - Added UmbraWG-specific attributes: `JC`, `Jmin`, `Jmax`, `S1`..`S4`,
   `H1`..`H4`, `I1`..`I5`, `DataInit`, `DataResponse`, `DataConfirm`,
   `DataTransport`.
 - Exposed `pub mod constants` with kernel flags.
 - Added 7 new unit tests and 3 integration tests for Linux.
 - Added GitHub Actions CI with UmbraWG kernel module.

### Bug fixes
 - Fixed clippy warnings (needless borrow, op_ref, await_holding_lock).

## [0.1.0] - 2026-06-06
### Breaking changes
 - Forked from `netlink-packet-wireguard` to support UmbraWG.

### New features
 - Generic netlink packet definitions for Umbra WireGuard.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-01-26
### Breaking changes
 - Rewrite to align with netlink-packet-route code style. (3067a39)
     - All netlink attribute are marked as `#[non_exhaustive]`.
     - Renamed `Wireguard` to `WireguardMessage`.
     - Renamed `WgDeviceAttrs` to `WireguardAttribute`.
     - Renamed `WgAllowedIp` to `WireguardAllowedIp`.
     - Renamed `WgPeerAttrs` to `WireguardPeer`.
     - Renamed `WgPeer` to `WireguardPeerAttribute`.
     - Will not expose any constants.
     - Changed the use of `std::time::SystemTime` to self-defined
       `WireguardTimeSpec`.
     - Do not raise error for unknown attribute but store in
       `Self::Other(DefaultNla)`.

